# Using plyEngine with vcpkg
# 1. Prefer the repo-as-registry flow (packaging/README.md): add a
#    vcpkg-configuration.json that lists github.com/plyndra/plyEngine as a
#    git registry scoped to packages: ["plyengine"], then plain manifest
#    installs resolve it:
#
#      vcpkg install plyengine
#
#    An overlay also works while the port is not in the registry:
#
#      vcpkg install plyengine --overlay-ports=packaging/vcpkg/port
#
# 2. Consume it from CMake:
#
#      find_package(plyEngine CONFIG REQUIRED)
#      target_link_libraries(mygame PRIVATE plyEngine::plyEngine)
#
# 3. vcpkg's dependencies are found automatically; the engine's own install
#    tree brings SDL3, glm and nlohmann_json along because they appear in its
#    public headers.

plyEngine::plyEngine provides the engine plus the internal archives it links
(glad, stb_impl, miniaudio_impl). Crow/asio, mdns, stb and miniaudio are
header-only and compiled into the engine, so they are not part of your link
line.

See docs/BUILDING.md#installing-the-engine-find_package for the equivalent
manual install.
